<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss palladium exports jump in February.</title>
<headline>Swiss palladium exports jump in February.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss exports of unfinished palladium rose to 21,500 kg in February from 4,828 kg the month before, according to provisional monthly trade figures from the Federal Customs Office.</p>
<p>				    Feb 1997	Jan 1997	Feb 1996</p>
<p> Exports (in kilograms)     21,500	  4,828	   1,407</p>
<p> Imports (in kilograms)     298	     318	     909</p>
<p>The biggest receiver of Swiss palladium exports was the United States with 15,535 kg in February versus 1,930 kg the month before.</p>
<p>The biggest source of imports was South Africa with 171 kg after 131 kg in January.</p>
<p>Switzerland is an international centre for precious metals smelting nad traders say a big part of the palladium movement is scrap coming in for refining into bars.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
